         "Translate concept by concept, not word by word: write the Urdu concept, find its standard English academic term (from a textbook, a bilingual abstract, or by asking a teacher), then collect that term's synonyms like any other concept. Many Pakistani journals publish abstracts in both languages, which makes them excellent term sources. English remains the main searching language of the big databases, so this translation step unlocks them.",
         "Concept by concept translate karein, lafz ba lafz nahi: Urdu concept likhein, is ka standard English academic term dhundein (textbook se, bilingual abstract se, ya teacher se pooch kar), phir us term ke synonyms kisi bhi doosre concept ki tarah jama karein. Bohat se Pakistani journals dono languages mein abstracts publish karte hain, jo unhein behtareen term sources banata hai. English bari databases ki main searching language rehti hai, is liye yeh translation step unhein unlock karta hai.",
